      "mechanism": "Establishes a post-election identity verification step before a provisional ballot can be processed.",
      "certainty": "stated"
    }
  ],
  "analysis": [
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "answer": "Under current law, voters verify their identity by stating their name and address and signing a poll book. This clause changes the process to require presenting a current government-issued photo ID.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§2",
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "answer": "Direct costs include administrative expenses for processing provisional ballots. Opportunity costs include the time and transportation required for voters to travel to the county clerk's office within the six-day window.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "answer": "The costs fall on voters who do not currently possess a valid government-issued photo ID and must spend time obtaining one. The benefits accrue to individuals and organizations prioritizing stricter in-person identity verification at the polls.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§2",
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "answer": "Political campaigns and advocacy groups will likely shift resources toward educating voters about ID requirements and organizing efforts to help provisional voters cure their ballots during the six-day window.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "answer": "It addresses the potential for in-person voter impersonation by requiring a photo ID. However, it creates a barrier to entry for voters who lack qualifying identification or face hurdles obtaining it.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§2",
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "answer": "County clerks gain the administrative duty and discretion to verify IDs presented during the six-day post-election period and determine if provisional ballots may be counted.",
      "disputed": false
    }
  ],
